# Agora — licensing

Agora is free software, licensed **per artifact**. This file is the umbrella; each
component repository carries the same arrangement plus the full licence texts.

## The split

| Artifact | Licence |
|---|---|
| **Libraries** — `libagora-base`, `libagora-app`, `libagora-drawing`, `libagora-text`, `libagora-iconservices`, `libagora-launchservices`, `libagora-watch` | **GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later** |
| **Programs** — `window-server`, `workspace`, `tests/` within the library repositories, `demo/*.sh` | **GNU General Public License, version 3 or later** |
| **Umbrella** — this superproject's own text, `release/` packaging | **GNU General Public License, version 3 or later** |
| **Third-party trees and assets** — see `THIRD-PARTY.md` | **their own upstream licences, unchanged** |

Every first-party source file states the identifier that applies to it:

```
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later   # libraries
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later    # programs
```

## Licence texts

- `COPYING` — GNU General Public License, version 3.
- `COPYING.LESSER` — GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3. This is the
  *additional permissions* text that sits on top of `COPYING`. LGPL-3.0 is not a
  standalone document, which is why both files are present.

Both are verbatim copies of the canonical texts published by the Free Software
Foundation at <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>. Do not edit them.

## Why version 3 and not 2.1

`libagora-core` and `libagora-dispatch` are Apache-2.0 extractions of Apple's
swift-corelibs, and every Agora binary links them. Apache-2.0 is compatible with
GPL-3.0/LGPL-3.0 only — it is incompatible with GPL-2.0 and LGPL-2.1. Version 3 is
therefore the only copyleft the combined work can resolve as.

## Third-party components

`libagora-objc` (MIT), `libagora-core` and `libagora-dispatch` (Apache-2.0),
`libagora-lcms2` (MIT), the Frost icon theme (MIT) and the default font set
(SIL OFL 1.1 / Apache-2.0) keep their upstream licences and notices. They are **not**
covered by Agora's licence and must not be relabelled. `THIRD-PARTY.md` is the register.

## History

Before 2026-10-22 the project was MIT licensed. Commits from before that date remain
available under MIT; the change is forward-only and no release was ever tagged. See
`LICENSE-CHANGE.md`.
